```sql
CREATE TABLE clicks (id bigint, ts timestamptz NOT NULL, ...)
  PARTITION BY RANGE (ts);
CREATE TABLE events_2026_04 PARTITION OF clicks
  FOR VALUES FROM ('2026-04-01') TO ('2026-05-01');
CREATE INDEX ON clicks USING brin (ts);
```

Avoid moving to a different database, or sharding in the application here — Concretely: range partitioning prunes whole partitions at plan time and turns retention into `DROP TABLE` instead of a long `DELETE`. BRIN suits naturally-ordered timestamps at a fraction of a b-tree's size.

